	// release that restarts the source from its failure. It re-executes the
	// source's tasks that did not succeed (failed, cancelled or skipped) whose
	// node the live schedule still holds, the live schedule's nodes the source
	// never ran, every descendant of those and, with include_changed_upstream,
	// every changed node upstream of anything it re-executes, until no changed
	// ancestor is left out. A node is changed when its content_hash, node_type,
	// secret_ref or upstream nodes differ between the live release and the
	// release the source's result for the node was built on: the source's
	// release, or for a success the source inherited, the release of the run
	// that built it. image_tag alone is not a change. Every other source
	// success is inherited. The new run keeps the source's schedule_name. A
	// non-empty expected_release_id must name the live release.
	// Errors:
	//
	//	NOT_FOUND           - source_run_id names no run.
	//	FAILED_PRECONDITION - the source is not failed or cancelled; or it has
	//	                      no task that did not succeed; or its schedule
	//	                      already has an active run; or it names no release,
	//	                      is a test run, or leaves nothing to re-execute; or
	//	                      the live release is not expected_release_id
	//	                      (message "the live release changed; preview
	//	                      again").
	//	ALREADY_EXISTS      - request_id reused with different parameters.
	//	UNAVAILABLE         - maintenance mode is on.
	TriggerRebase(context.Context, *TriggerRebaseRequest) (*TriggerRebaseResponse, error)
	// PreviewRebase reports what TriggerRebase would run for the same
	// source_run_id and include_changed_upstream on the live release, without
	// creating a run: the live release, how many nodes run and why, and the
	// changed upstream nodes with what each feeds and its last successful
	// duration. changed_nodes lists every changed upstream node the option would
	// add, whether or not include_changed_upstream is set. Maintenance mode does
	// not refuse it.
